  "id": "intersensory-perception",
  "term": "intersensory perception",
  "definition": "Intersensory perception is the ability to detect that information from different senses, such as what is seen and what is heard, belongs together. In this context, it refers to perceiving the relation between auditory and visual speech, including matching a speaker’s visible mouth movements with the corresponding sounds.",
